From f76bba6adbd157ec4ef5c54d6af3b93315bb4fd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:24:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] guest: authorize encrypted workspaces through measured policy

Authorize disk identity, key, filesystem, initialization and per-container
mount identity from measured initdata before device operations. Required mounts cannot disappear with host annotations. Use the disk ID for the guest
mount and CDH mapper so host aliases cannot reopen the same filesystem.
Verify the mapping and mount access before forwarding the container request.

Track and release acquired encrypted-workspace resources on preparation,
agent and sandbox cleanup paths. Keep ordinary cloud volumes on their
existing sandbox-lifetime mount path, including waits and filesystem
fallback. Workspace ownership and mount validation apply only when the
encrypted-volume profile is enabled.

Signed-off-by: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
